---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/') ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : import.meta.env.BASE_URL + '/';
---
<Base
  title="dsh-agent-plugins-market — One-stop skills, subagent, MCP and LSP manager for DeepSeek Harness"
  description="Manage skills, subagents, MCP services and LSP servers inside DeepSeek Harness (DSH), compatible with Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Kimi and other agent plugin layouts."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Your agent toolkit, inside DeepSeek Harness</h1>
    <p class="tagline">
      <strong>A one-stop skills, subagent, MCP and LSP manager inside DeepSeek Harness (DSH), compatible with Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Kimi and other agent plugin layouts.</strong>
    </p>
    <p class="lead">
      Reuse Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and Kimi suites, manage your own resources, and inspect running services in one workspace. Supported layouts are read in place without converting manifests or manually copying files.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a class="cta" href={`${base}install/`}>Get started</a>
      <a class="cta ghost" href="https://github.com/Sivan757/dsh-agent-plugins-market">GitHub</a>
      <a class="cta ghost" href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-agent-plugins-market">npm</a>
    </p>
    <img class="shot" src={`${base}assets/screenshot-workspace.png`} alt="The Agent Plugins workspace inside the DeepSeek Harness Web GUI" width="100%" />
  </section>

  <h2>What it solves</h2>
  <p>
    Add sources and install suites, create your own skills, commands and personas, and keep project-native resources in place. The workspace groups Market, Skills, Commands, Agent personas, MCP services, LSP servers and Hooks into seven tabs.
  </p>

  <h2>Highlights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Any skill repository works.</strong> A Git repository holding <code>skills/&lt;name&gt;/SKILL.md</code> is discovered as a suite with no manifest to add.</li>
    <li><strong>MCP OAuth with nothing to declare.</strong> A remote MCP server that answers <code>401</code> starts RFC 9728 discovery, dynamic client registration and PKCE authorization in your browser. OAuth is on by default.</li>
    <li><strong>Per-server MCP control.</strong> Override a declaration without editing its source, switch one tool off, and set the tool-call and startup timeouts.</li>
    <li><strong>Project resources on a switch.</strong> Turn on <strong>Scan project Agent layouts</strong> to read skills, commands, roles, MCP servers and hooks from the project's own directories.</li>
    <li><strong>Per-workspace control.</strong> Each workspace switches the six mounted surfaces, keeps its own filters, and saves a resource-window setup as a favorite.</li>
    <li><strong>Bilingual by default.</strong> Descriptions and documents show the original, a translation or both, and stay cached until you clear them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Supported plugin layouts</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Layout</th><th>Manifest</th></tr>
    <tr><td><a href="https://agent-plugins.org">agent-plugins</a></td><td><code>plugin.json</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Claude Code market</td><td><code>.claude-plugin/marketplace.json</code> + <code>.claude-plugin/plugin.json</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Universal</td><td><code>.plugin/plugin.json</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Cursor</td><td><code>.cursor-plugin/plugin.json</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Kimi</td><td><code>.kimi-plugin/plugin.json</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Codex</td><td><code>.codex-plugin/plugin.json</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Skill collection</td><td>none (flat <code>SKILL.md</code> directories)</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Quick install</h2>
  <p>In the DSH Web GUI, open <strong>Plugins</strong> in the sidebar, press <strong>Add plugin</strong>, and enter <code>dsh-agent-plugins-market</code>. Then restart DSH and open <strong>Settings → Agent Plugins</strong>.</p>
  <p>From a terminal instead:</p>
  <pre><code>dsh plugin --profile &lt;name&gt; add dsh-agent-plugins-market</code></pre>
  <p>Requires Node.js 22 or later and a DSH Web profile with the skill service. The <a href="https://github.com/Sivan757/dsh-agent-plugins-market">README</a> lists the DSH host packages this plugin declares; feature availability depends on host services. See the <a href={`${base}install/`}>install guide</a> for details.</p>

  <h2>Learn more</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={`${base}install/`}>Step-by-step install guide</a></li>
    <li><a href={`${base}compatible-plugins/`}>Known compatible plugin marketplaces</a></li>
    <li><a href={`${base}faq/`}>FAQ</a></li>
  </ul>
</Base>
